Okay, I really like the IBMGraphics chars, and having used them for years,
they are also what I'm used to.  However, it's really a pain getting them
working for various platforms (e.g. I've so far been unsuccessful in OS X).

I also don't like the "non standardness" of them, for possibly dubious
ideological reasons.

However, I'd prefer not to switch to plain ASCII; I think the line drawing
characters add a lot, for example in the gnomish mines, where they make it
much easier for me to determine what has already been explored.

So, I've been considering having a go at DEC graphics.  
Questions:  
- do these suffer less from being a "broken, obsolete standard"?
- can anyone who uses them recommend a nice font and settings to use?  I
  like playing with a nice large font, so that an 80x24 window fills a good
  portion of my screen.  For IBMGraphics, I'm currently using vga11x19.  I
  guess this doesn't matter if it's a TrueType or postscript font.
- does anyone who uses DEC have a setting that allows you to see lit
  vs. unlit corridors?

Is there some better standard character set, besides cp437 and DEC, that has
line drawing characters, that would be worth implementing in NetHack?

